      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "<p>(1 in a multiple picture album)\nThis is a stock photo of a California Condor in flight. When you see them sitting they are just a blob of black and they don't look that large. There is not much beauty to them. Their face is one only a mother could love.\n</p>\nBUT . . . when they fly, they are beautiful. I watched one soar over the Grand Canyon last week. He was something to see.  When he had enough of soaring, he tucked in his wings and dive bombed down to a ledge, opening his wings again only just before landing. Amazing thing!",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
      },
